-- Ravi: a dialect of Lua 5.3 with optional static typing, an LLVM JIT and an ahead-of-time
-- compiler. Luarust's design almost exactly, arrived at first and written in C -- which is
-- the argument for it being in the standard set rather than a curiosity.
--
-- Ravi runs unannotated Lua too; the annotation is the point of comparison, because it is
-- what its JIT reads to pick a type-specific bytecode, exactly as `Op::Binary` carries a
-- type here.
local sum: integer = 0
for i = 1, ITERATIONS do
    sum = (sum + i) % 1000000007
end
print(sum)
